{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>For as for the Egyptians whom you have seen today, you shall never see them again</b> — According to the opinion of our Sages, this is a negative commandment for all generations (Mekhilta ad loc.). If so, Scripture says: <b>Fear not</b>, <b>stand still</b> in your place, and <b>see the salvation of HaShem</b> — that He will save you today from their hand, and do not return to their service. For as for the Egyptians whom you see today, the Holy One, blessed be He, further commands you not to willingly see them again from now and forever; and this would be a commandment from the mouth of Moses to Israel, not mentioned earlier [in the verse]. And so too: \"Nor shall he cause the people to return to Egypt, to multiply horses, and HaShem has said to you: You shall never again return by this way\" (Deuteronomy 17:16) — this is truly a commandment, not a promise."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:07:45.175787404Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}